From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kemp233 <kemp233@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 13:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(lb2004-rk3566): add CONFIG_TARGET_EVB_RK3568 to defconfig
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The kemp233/u-boot-1@rockchip-v2026.01 lb2004-rk3566_defconfig is
incomplete - it does not set CONFIG_TARGET_EVB_RK3568=y, which is
required for the build to find the board/rockchip/evb_rk3568/evb_rk3568.c
board file. Without this, the build silently fails during "make
olddefconfig" with:

  Error: No board selected. Please check your board configuration.

The fix is to explicitly set CONFIG_TARGET_EVB_RK3568=y in the defconfig.
This is the same TARGET used by z96a (which also runs on rk3568 board
framework since rk3566 and rk3568 share the same SoC IP block).

---
 configs/lb2004-rk3566_defconfig | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/configs/lb2004-rk3566_defconfig
+++ b/configs/lb2004-rk3566_defconfig
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 CONFIG_ARM=y
 CONFIG_SKIP_LOWLEVEL_INIT=y
 CONFIG_COUNTER_FREQUENCY=24000000
+CONFIG_TARGET_EVB_RK3568=y
 CONFIG_ARCH_ROCKCHIP=y
 CONFIG_SF_DEFAULT_SPEED=24000000
 CONFIG_SF_DEFAULT_MODE=0x2000
-- 
2.30.0

